the shoot apex of <italic>Datura stramonium</italic> during transition to flowering</article-title><source>American Journal of Botany</source><year>1969</year><volume>56</volume><fpage>1127</fpage><lpage>1134</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="bib10"><element-citation publication-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cutter</surname><given-names>EG</given-names></name></person-group><source>Plant anatomy: experiment and interpretation. Part 2. Organs</source><year>1971</year><publisher-loc>London</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Edward Arnold (Publishers) Ltd</publisher-name></element-citation></ref><ref id="bib11"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dumais</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Kwiatkowska</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Analysis of surface growth in shoot apices</article-title><source>The Plant Journal</source><year>2002</year><volume>31</volume><fpage>229</fpage><lpage>241</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12121452</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="bib12"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Grandjean</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Vernoux</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Laufs</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Belcram</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Mizukami</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Traas</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title><italic>In vivo</italic> analysis of cell division, cell growth, and differentiation at the shoot apical meristem in <italic>Arabidopsis</italic></article-title><source>The Plant Cell</source><year>2004</year><volume>16</volume><fpage>74</fpage><lpage>87</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14671026</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Green</surname><given-names>PB</given-names></name><name><surname>Havelange</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Bernier</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Floral morphogenesis in <italic>Anagallis</italic>: scanning-electron-micrograph sequences from individual growing meristems before, during, and after the transition to flowering</article-title><source>Planta</source><year>1991</year><volume>185</volume><fpage>502</fpage><lpage>512</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Green</surname><given-names>PB</given-names></name><name><surname>Erickson</surname><given-names>RO</given-names></name><name><surname>Richmond</surname><given-names>PA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>On the physical basis of cell morphogenesis</article-title><source>Annals of the New York Academy of Sciences</source><year>1970</year><volume>175</volume><fpage>712</fpage><lpage>731</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="bib15"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hepworth</surname><given-names>SR</given-names></name><name><surname>Klenz</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name><name><surname>Haughn</surname><given-names>GW</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>UFO in the <italic>Arabidopsis</italic> inflorescence apex is required for floral-meristem identity and bract suppression</article-title><source>Planta</source><year>2006</year><volume>223</volume><fpage>769</fpage><lpage>778</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16244866</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="bib16"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kwiatkowska</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Ontogenetic changes of phyllotaxis in <italic>Anagallis arvensis</italic> L</article-title><source>Acta Societatis Botanicorum Poloniae</source><year>1995</year><volume>64</volume><fpage>319</fpage><lpage>325</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="bib17"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kwiatkowska</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Intraspecific variation of phyllotactic stability in <italic>Anagallis arvensis</italic></article-title><source>Acta Societatis Botanicorum Poloniae</source><year>1997</year><volume>66</volume><fpage>259</fpage><lpage>271</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="bib18"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kwiatkowska</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Surface growth at the reproductive shoot apex of <italic>Arabidopsis thaliana</italic>: <italic>pin-formed 1</italic> and wild type</article-title><source>Journal of Experimental Botany</source><year>2004a</year><volume>55</volume><fpage>1021</fpage><lpage>1032</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15020634</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="bib19"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kwiatkowska</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Structural integration at the shoot apical meristem: models, measurements and experiments</article-title><source>American Journal of Botany</source><year>2004b</year><volume>91</volume><fpage>1277</fpage><lpage>1293</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="bib20"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kwiatkowska</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Flower primordium formation at the <italic>Arabidopsis</italic> shoot apex: quantitative analysis of surface geometry and growth</article-title><source>Journal of Experimental Botany</source><year>2006</year><volume>57</volume><fpage>571</fpage><lpage>580</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16377735</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="bib21"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kwiatkowska</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Flowering and apical meristem growth dynamics</article-title><source>Journal of Experimental Boany</source><year>2008</year><volume>59</volume><fpage>187</fpage><lpage>201</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="bib22"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kwiatkowska</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Dumais</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Growth and morphogenesis at the vegetative shoot apex of <italic>Anagallis arvensis</italic> L</article-title><source>Journal of Experimental Botany</source><year>2003</year><volume>54</volume><fpage>1585</fpage><lpage>1595</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12730267</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="bib23"><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Laufs</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Grandjean</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Jonak</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Ki&#x000ea;u</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Traas</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Cellular parameters of the shoot apical meristem in <italic>Arabidopsis</italic></article-title><source>The Plant Cell</source><year>1998</year><volume>10</volume><fpage>1375</fpage><lpage>1389</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9707536</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="bib24"